Description: hw/block: Add the i.MX21 NAND flash controller
 The NFC with its four page buffers and a small-page NAND chip behind it
 (64 MiB, ID 0xAD 0x76 by default). The chip's contents come from a block
 backend in nanddump's layout, 528-byte records of page data then spare
 bytes; programs and erases are written back unless the drive is
 read-only.
 .
 The contents are a copy of the drive, read at realize, and are not in
 the migration stream. loadvm and -loadvm restore the drive (with
 -loadvm, after the copy was read), so after a restore the contents are
 read again from a writable drive when the machine next runs: during the
 load the drive is drained (loadvm) or not yet active (an incoming
 migration). Without a writable drive the contents are only in memory
 and are kept as they are. The load refuses a page, column, area or
 address count out of range; each indexes the chip's contents or its
 address bytes.
Author: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AI generated code]
Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Fc77Z6fVVe4rWJxPT
